.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-DEPS 1
.Os Wattle DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-deps
.Nd manage the dependencies of a project
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "wattle deps"
.Ar verb
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Manage the dependencies of the project in the current directory.
Nothing is installed under
.Ql "*prefix*" .
A build made without the OS library does not include
.Cm deps ,
and each verb exits with status 1 after saying so.
.Ic d
is a synonym for
.Cm deps .
.
.Sh VERBS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Cm vendor
.Xc
Copy the entries of
.Ql ":vendored"
in
.Ql "info\&.edn"
in the current directory into the current directory.
Each entry is a map with a
.Ql ":name"
and a
.Ql ":url" ,
which is a source as for
.Cm install
in
.Xr wattle-apps 1 .
It may have a
.Ql ":ref" ,
a branch or tag for a Git repository,
a
.Ql ":prefix" ,
the directory to copy into,
which is the current directory by default,
and
.Ql ":paths" ,
a vector of the paths to copy.
A path is a string,
or a vector of a path in the source and a path under the
.Ql ":prefix" .
The whole source is copied if there is no
.Ql ":paths" .
A file that is already there is replaced.
No path may be absolute or contain
.Ql "\&.\&." .
Every entry is checked before any is fetched,
and no two may have the same
.Ql ":name" .
.Cm vendor
records no revision,
because the copies belong to the project.
See VENDORING in
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Copy the vendored sources that
.Ql "info\&.edn"
lists into the current directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle deps vendor
.Ed
.
